    "source": "Pieter Wesseling",
    "copyright": "",
    "tablehtml": "<table class=\"MsoNormalTable\" style=\"border-collapse: collapse;\" border=\"0\" width=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\">\r\n<tbody>\r\n<tr style=\"page-break-inside: avoid; height: 25.35pt;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 116.95pt; border: none; border-top: solid black 1.0pt; background: #8DB3E2; padding: 0cm 0cm 0cm 0cm; height: 25.35pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"156\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3.0pt 5.8pt 3.0pt 4.2pt;\"><strong>&nbsp;</strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 116.95pt; border: none; border-top: solid black 1.0pt; background: #8DB3E2; padding: 0cm 0cm 0cm 0cm; height: 25.35pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"156\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin-left: 4.7pt;\"><strong>Diffuse paediatric-type high-grade glioma</strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 116.95pt; border: none; border-top: solid black 1.0pt; background: #8DB3E2; padding: 0cm 0cm 0cm 0cm; height: 25.35pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"156\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3.0pt 4.5pt 3.0pt 5.45pt;\"><strong>Diffuse paediatric-type low-grade glioma</strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 116.95pt; border: none; border-top: solid black 1.0pt; background: #8DB3E2; padding: 0cm 0cm 0cm 0cm; height: 25.35pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"156\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin-left: 7.1pt;\"><strong>Circumscribed astrocytic glioma</strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 116.95pt; border: none; border-top: solid black 1.0pt; background: #8DB3E2; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt; height: 25.35pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"156\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong>Glioneuronal and neuronal tumours</strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 116.95pt; border: none; border-top: solid black 1.0pt; background: #8DB3E2; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt; height: 25.35pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"156\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Adult-type diffuse glioma</p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"page-break-inside: avoid; height: 25.35pt;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 116.95pt; padding: 0cm 0cm 0cm 0cm; height: 25.35pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"156\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3.0pt 5.8pt 3.0pt 4.2pt;\"><strong>Tumours typically presenting in children</strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 116.95pt; padding: 0cm 0cm 0cm 0cm; height: 25.35pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"156\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin-left: 4.7pt;\"><strong>Diffuse midline glioma, H3 K27&ndash;altered<sup>a</sup></strong></p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin-left: 4.7pt;\"><strong>Diffuse paediatric-type high-grade glioma, H3-wildtype and IDH-wildtype<sup>a</sup></strong></p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin-left: 4.7pt;\"><strong>Infant-type hemispheric glioma<sup>a</sup></strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 116.95pt; padding: 0cm 0cm 0cm 0cm; height: 25.35pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"156\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3.0pt 4.5pt 3.0pt 5.45pt;\"><strong>Diffuse astrocytoma, <em>MYB</em>- or <em>MYBL1</em>-altered<sup>a</sup></strong></p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3.0pt 4.5pt 3.0pt 5.45pt;\"><strong>Angiocentric glioma<sup>a</sup></strong></p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3.0pt 4.5pt 3.0pt 5.45pt;\"><strong>Diffuse low-grade glioma, MAPK pathway&ndash;altered<sup>a</sup></strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 116.95pt; padding: 0cm 0cm 0cm 0cm; height: 25.35pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"156\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin-left: 7.1pt;\"><strong>Subependymal giant cell astrocytoma<sup>a</sup></strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 116.95pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt; height: 25.35pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"156\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong>Desmoplastic infantile ganglioglioma&nbsp;/ desmoplastic infantile astrocytoma<sup>a</sup></strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 116.95pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt; height: 25.35pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"156\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">&nbsp;</p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"page-break-inside: avoid; height: 25.35pt;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 116.95pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 0cm 0cm 0cm; height: 25.35pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"156\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3.0pt 5.8pt 3.0pt 4.2pt;\"><strong>Tumours that may present in children or adults</strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 116.95pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 0cm 0cm 0cm; height: 25.35pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"156\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin-left: 4.7pt;\"><strong>Diffuse hemispheric glioma, H3 G34&ndash;mutant<sup>a</sup></strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 116.95pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 0cm 0cm 0cm; height: 25.35pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"156\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3.0pt 4.5pt 3.0pt 5.45pt;\"><strong>Polymorphous low-grade neuroepithelial tumour of the young<sup>a</sup></strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 116.95pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 0cm 0cm 0cm; height: 25.35pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"156\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin-left: 7.1pt;\"><strong>Pilocytic astrocytoma<sup>a</sup></strong></p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin-left: 7.1pt;\"><strong>Pleomorphic xanthoastrocytoma<sup>a</sup></strong></p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin-left: 7.1pt;\"><strong>Astroblastoma, <em>MN1</em>-altered<sup>a</sup></strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 116.95pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt; height: 25.35pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"156\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong>Ganglioglioma<sup>a</sup></strong></p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong>Dysembryoplastic neuroepithelial tumour<sup>a</sup></strong></p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong>DGONC<sup>a</sup></strong></p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Papillary glioneuronal tumour</p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Rosette-forming glioneuronal tumour</p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Myxoid glioneuronal tumour</p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong>Diffuse leptomeningeal glioneuronal tumour<sup>a</sup></strong></p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong>Multinodular and vacuolating neuronal tumour<sup>a</sup></strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 116.95pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt; height: 25.35pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"156\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">&nbsp;</p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"page-break-inside: avoid; height: 25.35pt;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 116.95pt; border: none; border-bottom: solid windowtext 1.0pt; padding: 0cm 0cm 0cm 0cm; height: 25.35pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"156\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3.0pt 5.8pt 3.0pt 4.2pt;\">Tumours typically presenting in adulthood</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 116.95pt; border: none; border-bottom: solid windowtext 1.0pt; padding: 0cm 0cm 0cm 0cm; height: 25.35pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"156\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin-left: 4.7pt;\">&nbsp;</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 116.95pt; border: none; border-bottom: solid windowtext 1.0pt; padding: 0cm 0cm 0cm 0cm; height: 25.35pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"156\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3.0pt 4.5pt 3.0pt 5.45pt;\">&nbsp;</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 116.95pt; border: none; border-bottom: solid windowtext 1.0pt; padding: 0cm 0cm 0cm 0cm; height: 25.35pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"156\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin-left: 7.1pt;\">Chordoid glioma</p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin-left: 7.1pt;\">High-grade astrocytoma with piloid features</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 116.95pt; border: none; border-bottom: solid windowtext 1.0pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt; height: 25.35pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"156\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Gangliocytoma</p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Dysplastic cerebellar gangliocytoma (Lhermitte&ndash;Duclos disease)</p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Central neurocytoma</p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Extraventricular neurocytoma</p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Cerebellar liponeurocytoma</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 116.95pt; border: none; border-bottom: solid windowtext 1.0pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt; height: 25.35pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"156\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Astrocytoma, IDH-mutant</p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Oligodendroglioma, IDH-mutant and 1p/19q-codeleted</p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Glioblastoma, IDH-wildtype</p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n</tbody>\r\n</table>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">DGONC, diffuse glioneuronal tumour with oligodendroglioma-like features and nuclear clusters.</p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><sup>a</sup>These tumours (also indicated in bold) are more extensively discussed in this volume on paediatric tumours; please refer to the WHO classification of CNS tumours for the other tumour types.</p>",
